.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_DC_RETURN_DEV_STATE 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_dc_return_dev_state ,
.Nm ndi_dc_return_ap_state ,
.Nm ndi_dc_return_bus_state
.Nd copy device-control state to the requesting process
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_dc_return_dev_state
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "struct devctl_iocdata *dcp"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_dc_return_ap_state
.Fa "devctl_ap_state_t *ap"
.Fa "struct devctl_iocdata *dcp"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_dc_return_bus_state
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "struct devctl_iocdata *dcp"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dip
Device to report, or bus nexus for the bus-state function.
.It Va dcp
Copied device-control request containing the user output address.
.It Va ap
Attachment-point state in kernel memory.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions copy state to the user output buffer recorded in a request
returned by \fBndi_dc_allochdl()\fP.
\fBndi_dc_return_dev_state()\fP reports the supplied device's state, using
\fBDEVICE_OFFLINE\fP, \fBDEVICE_DOWN\fP, or \fBDEVICE_ONLINE\fP, with \fBDEVICE_BUSY\fP
also set when an online device is referenced.
Here \fBdip\fP is the device itself, not its parent.
.Pp
\fBndi_dc_return_bus_state()\fP obtains the bus state using \fBndi_get_bus_state()\fP
and copies it to the output buffer.
\fBndi_dc_return_ap_state()\fP copies a caller-supplied attachment-point state,
converting it for a 32-bit caller when necessary.
.Pp
New device-state handlers can use \fBndi_devctl_ioctl()\fP or
\fBndi_devctl_device_getstate()\fP to resolve the child named in the request.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions must be called from user context.
Device-state reporting may sleep.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP on success, \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP for
invalid arguments or failure to obtain the state, and \fBNDI_FAULT\fP for a
copyout failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_dc_allochdl 9F ,
.Xr ndi_devctl_ioctl 9F ,
.Xr ndi_get_bus_state 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
